ensors_of_format_3_3_over_prime_fields)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago;   * Murray Bremner ... For each canonical form, we determine the size of its orbit and the rank of the arrays in its orbit. ... For any ${P\\, \\in \\, \\mathbb{P}^{N}}$, the symmetric tensor rank sr(P) is the minimal cardinality of a set ${\\mathcal{S} \\subset \\nu_{d}(\\mathbb{P}^{r})}$ spanning P.\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nCanonical forms of 2 × 2 × 2 and 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 arrays over 𝔽2and 𝔽3\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Jul 2013\n  * LINEAR MULTILINEAR A\n\n  * Murray Bremner\n  * Stavros Georgios Stavrou\n\nWe consider arrays of size 2 × 2 × 2 and 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 over the fields with two and three elements. We use computer algebra to determine the canonical forms of these arrays with respect to the action of the semidirect product of general linear groups with the symmetric group. For each canonical form, we determine the size of its orbit and the rank of the arrays in its orbit.\n\nView\n\nShow abstract\n\nReal and Complex Rank for Real Symmetric Tensors with Low Ranks\n\nArticle\n\nFull-text available\n\n  * Jan 2013\n\n  * Edoardo Ballico\n  * Alessandra Bernardi\n\nWe study the case of a real homogeneous polynomial P whose minimal real and complex decompositions in terms of powers of linear forms are different. We prove that, if the sum of the complex and the real ranks of P is at most $\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nau:Bremner_M in:math - SciRate Search (https://scirate.com/search?q=au%3ABremner_M+in%3Amath)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; ~Bremner}, title = {{T}ernary analogs of dendriform algebras and quadri-algebras}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2610.37848}, note = {arXiv:2610.37848v1} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... When the unary operators commute, we derive canonical representatives and effective recurrences, with corresponding monotonicity conditions in the combinatorial models. ... In special cases, the resulting sequences recover classical families including the Catalan numbers, the small Schröder numbers, and rooted-tree numbers. ... Using methods of computer algebra, especially Gröbner bases for submodules of free modules over polynomial rings, we solve a classification problem in theory of algebraic operads: we show that the only nontrivial (possibly inhomogeneous) distributive law between the operad of Lie algebras and the operad of commutative associative algebras is given by the Livernet-Loday formula deforming the Poisson operad into the associative operad. ... ~Bremner}, title = {{E}numeration and {A}symptotic {F}ormulas for {R}ectangular {P}artitions of the {H}ypercube}, year = {2019}, eprint = {1903.00813}, howpublished = {Journal of Integer Sequences 23 (2020) Article 20.1.4}, note = {arXiv:1903.00813v2} }[Button: Copy Citation] ... Bremner \\& Dotsenko introduced $C_{d,p}(n)$ in their work on Boardman--Vogt tensor products of operads; they used homological algebra to prove a recursive formula and a functional equation.\n\n63 results for au:Bremner_M in:math\n\nShow all abstracts\n\n  * Ternary analogs of dendriform algebras and quadri-algebras\n\nYu Hin Au, Murray R. Bremner\n\nOct 30 2026 math.RA math.CO arXiv:2610.37848v1\n\n@misc{2610.37848, author = {Yu Hin Au and Murray R.~Bremner}, title = {{T}ernary analogs of dendriform algebras and quadri-algebras}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2610.37848}, note = {arXiv:2610.37848v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe construct ternary analogs of dendriform algebras and quadri-algebras, generalizing the well-known binary case. These new structures are defined in terms of nonsymmetric operads. We construct these new operads using ternary operations defined in terms of ternary Rota-Baxter operators. The relations defining these operads lie in the quadratic subspace of the kernel of a rewriting morphism from a free operad to the operad generated by one associative ternary operation and one (or two commuting) unary operators satisfying the ternary Rota-Baxter relation(s). We use computational algebra to compute a basis for the quadratic component of the kernel and thereby obtain the quadratic relations which define these new operads. In the dendriform case, we obtain 3 operations satisfying 10 relations. In the quadri-algebra case, we obtain 9 operations satisfying 50 relations. The latter computations combine modular and rational arithmetic, but we are able to provide certificates of the results which can be verified in characteristic 0.\n\n  * Enumerating Multi-Operator Monomials in Commutative and Noncommutative Settings\n\nYu Hin Au, Murray R. Bremner\n\nApr 29 2026 math.CO arXiv:2604.25731v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2604.25731, author = {Yu Hin Au and Murray R.~Bremner}, title = {{E}numerating {M}ulti-{O}perator {M}onomials in {C}ommutative and {N}oncommutative {S}ettings}, year = {2026}, eprint = {2604.25731}, note = {arXiv:2604.25731v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe study enumeration problems for multi-operator monomials generated from one indeterminate by an associative multiplication together with finitely many unary operators. We consider four regimes, according to whether multiplication is commutative and whether the unary operators commute. In the case where the unary operators do not commute, we obtain explicit multigraded generating functions and coefficient formulas, including a multinomial refinement of the Narayana numbers, together with interpretations in terms of rooted trees, restricted lattice paths, and binary trees. When the unary operators commute, we derive canonical representatives and effective recurrences, with corresponding monotonicity conditions in the combinatorial models. When multiplication is commutative, the sequence decomposition is replaced by a multiset decomposition, leading to exp--log generating functions and Euler-transform recurrences. In special cases, the resulting sequences recover classical families including the Catalan numbers, the small Schröder numbers, and rooted-tree numbers.\n\n  * The Veronese square of the dendriform operad\n\nMurray R. Bremner\n\nDec 15 2025 math.RA math.CT arXiv:2512.11703v2\nWe use combinatorics of monomials and computational linear algebra to determine the kernel. We obtain 33 linearly independent quadratic relations satisfied by the Veronese square.\n\n  * Algebraic identities for linear operators on associative triple systems (long version)\n\nMurray R. Bremner\n\nDec 05 2025 math.RA math.OA arXiv:2512.04190v1\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{2512.04190, author = {Murray R.~Bremner}, title = {{A}lgebraic identities for linear operators on associative triple systems (long version)}, year = {2025}, eprint = {2512.04190}, note = {arXiv:2512.04190v1} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe present the first classification of algebraic identities in 3 variables for linear operators on associative structures. We work in the context of associative triple systems, but since any associative algebra with product $xy$ becomes an associative triple system with product $xyz$, our results apply to associative algebras as well. \nYu Hin Au, Fatemeh Bagherzadeh, Murray R. Bremner\n\nMar 05 2019 math.CO math.KT math.RA arXiv:1903.00813v2\n\n[Button: Scited][Button: Scite!]\n\n0\n\n@misc{1903.00813, author = {Yu Hin Au and Fatemeh Bagherzadeh and Murray R.~Bremner}, title = {{E}numeration and {A}symptotic {F}ormulas for {R}ectangular {P}artitions of the {H}ypercube}, year = {2019}, eprint = {1903.00813}, howpublished = {Journal of Integer Sequences 23 (2020) Article 20.1.4}, note = {arXiv:1903.00813v2} }[Button: Copy Citation]\n\nPDF\n\nWe study a two-parameter generalization of the Catalan numbers: $C_{d,p}(n)$ is the number of ways to subdivide the $d$-dimensional hypercube into $n$ rectangular blocks using orthogonal partitions of fixed arity $p$. Bremner \\& Dotsenko introduced $C_{d,p}(n)$ in their work on Boardman--Vogt tensor products of operads; they used homological algebra to prove a recursive formula and a functional equation. We express $C_{d,p}(n)$ as simple finite sums, and determine their growth rate and asymptotic behaviour. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nKIT - Institute of Stochastics - Research - List of publications (https://stoch.math.kit.edu/english/64.php)\nciteturn1search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Journal of the Royal Statistical Society / Series B, 78 (3), 545–546 ... Tensor Valuations and Their Applications in Stochastic Geometry and Imaging. ... Integral geometry and algebraic structures for tensor valuations\n\nHolzmann, H.; Klar, B.\nDiscussion of the paper: “Of quantiles and expectiles: consistent scoring functions, Choquet representations and forecast rankings\" [by W. Ehm, T. Gneiting, A. Jordan and F. Krüger]\n2017. Journal of the Royal Statistical Society / Series B, 78 (3), 545–546\n\nGoodey, P.; Hug, D.; Weil, W.\nKinematic formulas for area measures\n2017. Indiana University Mathematics Journal, 66 (3), 997–1018. doi:10.1512/iumj.2017.66.6047\n\nHug, D.; Schneider, R.\nTensor Valuations and Their Local Versions\n2017. Tensor Valuations and Their Applications in Stochastic Geometry and Imaging. Ed.: E.V. Jensen, 27–65, Springer International Publishing. doi:10.1007/978-3-319-51951-7_2\n\nHug, D.; Klatt, M. A.; Last, G.; Schulte, M.\nSecond Order Analysis of Geometric Functionals of Boolean Models\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFull Text Articles available from EurekaMag Chapter 83129 (https://partners.eurekamag.com/research/083/128/)\nciteturn1search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; 2020: Differential forms and quadrics of the canonical image. ... Journal of Pure and Applied Algebra 154(1-3): 257-264 Blair Perot, J. ... 1983: Differential formulation of the dynamic renormalisation group in the large-n limit.\n-